Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "DATE_VALID_STD": filters the calendar days that make‑up the required week in the prior year (2023‑01‑16 … 2023‑01‑22).  
• "POSTAL_CODE": identifies the U.S. ZIP code for which snowfall is reported – needed in SELECT list and GROUP / ORDER clauses.  
• "COUNTRY": allows us to keep only United States rows ("US").  
• "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN": daily total snowfall (inches) – use for the > 6‑inch filter and for reporting / aggregation.  
• "DOY_STD": optional helper column for day‑of‑year logic (DOY 16‑22 for 2023).  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows) that progress from very simple inspection to the fully‑formed answer.  
Every identifier is wrapped in double quotes and the canonical object path is used:  
GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY  

```sql
-- 1) Peek at January‑2023 records to understand date formatting
SELECT DISTINCT "DATE_VALID_STD"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-01' AND '2023-01-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Check a few snowfall values greater than 6 inches (any date, any country)
SELECT "POSTAL_CODE",
       "DATE_VALID_STD",
       "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) List distinct snowfall amounts over 6 inches within the target week
SELECT DISTINCT "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Count all U.S. rows in that week with snowfall > 6 inches
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "row_cnt"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6;
```

```sql
-- 5) Quick view of which ZIP codes appear (distinct)
SELECT DISTINCT "POSTAL_CODE"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Inspect day‑by‑day snowfall > 6 inches, ordered by ZIP then date
SELECT "POSTAL_CODE",
       "DATE_VALID_STD",
       "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "POSTAL_CODE", "DATE_VALID_STD"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Maximum single‑day snowfall for each ZIP during the week
SELECT "POSTAL_CODE",
       MAX("TOT_SNOWFALL_IN") AS "MAX_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
GROUP BY "POSTAL_CODE"
ORDER BY "MAX_SNOWFALL_IN" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Same as #6 but sorted by snowfall descending for quick spot‑check
SELECT "POSTAL_CODE",
       "DATE_VALID_STD",
       "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Add a row number per ZIP to see the ranking of daily snowfall sizes
SELECT "POSTAL_CODE",
       "DATE_VALID_STD",
       "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN",
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "POSTAL_CODE" 
                          ORDER BY "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" DESC) AS "rn_within_zip"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "POSTAL_CODE", "rn_within_zip"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final answer‑style query: every U.S. postal‑code / date pair
--     with daily snowfall > 6 inches during the target week
SELECT "POSTAL_CODE",
       "DATE_VALID_STD",
       "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" AS "SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE.HISTORY_DAY
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-16' AND '2023-01-22'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "POSTAL_CODE", "DATE_VALID_STD"
LIMIT 20;
```

